	"nodes":[
		{"id":"8a6ac187b079e234","x":-466,"y":-380,"width":386,"height":80,"type":"text","text":"# A new view on system strength - Watt Clarity\n\nArgues that GFL is not inherently bad, just different, and that a low inertia grid actually has many advantages when compared to a high inertia grid. We should focus instead on better transmission capability and optimising GFL to GFM ratio rather than imposing penalties on solar and wind projects for using GFL inverters. \n\nhttps://wattclarity.com.au/articles/2026/06/reframing-the-grid-discussion-from-system-strength-to-system-behaviour/?_gl=1*1uizbah*_ga*MTUyMDYyOTAyMy4xNzgwNTI2NzEy*_ga_4ZTT9PF6TR*czE3ODA1MjY3MTIkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODA1MjY3MTIkajYwJGwwJGgw"},
		{"id":"d602014597b26ba5","type":"text","text":"Au\n\nArticle talks about Australian renewable curtailment and how it had reached 7,200 GWh in 2025, doubling figure in 2024. Would be interesting to look more into the breakdown of this.\n\nhttps://reneweconomy.com.au/the-kardashev-scale-australias-staggering-energy-transition-and-its-untapped-opportunity/","x":-466,"y":-240,"width":386,"height":120}
